# Sheet and shared behaviours

- Local bricks live in `packages/ui/bricks/<name>/` (`*.def.ts` IR via `@ui8kit/codegen/bricks/_dsl`, `*.variants.json`, `data.json` showcase cases) and are appended to the upstream registry in `packages/ui/scripts/registry.ts`. Both runtimes are generated; parity must stay 0 mismatches.
- Lucide icons in bricks come from `bricks/_lucide.ts` (parsed lucide-static SVG) — no hand-copied paths.
- `Sheet` = `div role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-label` + `hidden` until open, overlay `data-ui8kit="sheet-overlay"`, panel slot. `SheetTrigger` has `aria-controls=<sheet id>`, `aria-expanded`, `aria-haspopup="dialog"`, menu/x icons switched by CSS on `[aria-expanded="true"]`. `SheetClose` closes the nearest sheet.
- Behaviour only in `packages/ui/behaviors/ui8kit.js` (no framework, event delegation on `data-ui8kit`): open portals the sheet to `<body>`, focuses the first focusable, traps Tab/Shift+Tab, Esc + overlay + SheetClose + link click close, focus returns to the trigger, `ui-sheet-locked` on `<html>` locks scroll, resize past the breakpoint closes. Never add per-app copies of this logic, never inline handlers.
- Site loads it as `/assets/ui8kit.js` (defer); design app imports it in `+layout.svelte` `onMount`.
- Usage: site navbar collapses below `lg` (1024px; decided by the user 2026-10-18 — do not move it to `md`, the full menu overflows at 768px) into `navbar-menu` (right); design app sidebar becomes `ds-nav-sheet` (left) below `lg`. Content inside the sheet is the same data as the desktop nav — no duplicated copy.
- Verify with `bun run test:behaviors` (both apps @390px) after any change.
